cat > /workspace/epic_breakdown.txt << 'EOF'
================================================================================
EPIC BREAKDOWN: Self-Service Report Export Feature
================================================================================
Initiative: REPORT_EXPORT
Epic ID: EXPORT_PACKAGE
Duration Target: 2-week sprint
Stakeholders: End Users, Administrators, Power Users

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EPIC SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Enable end users and administrators to export filtered reports to PDF and CSV
formats through a self-service interface, with audit trail capabilities for
administrators.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INVEST-COMPLIANT USER STORIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 1: End User - Basic Report Export
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As an End User,
I want to export reports to CSV format,
So that I can analyze the data in spreadsheet applications.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Can be developed and tested separately
- Negotiable: Format options can be discussed
- Valuable: Directly addresses user need for data analysis
- Estimable: Clear scope for CSV generation
- Small: Single format export
- Testable: Acceptance criteria clearly defined

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in as an End User
  When I navigate to a report with data
  Then I see an "Export to CSV" button
  When I click "Export to CSV"
  Then the report data downloads as a CSV file
  And the CSV contains all visible columns and rows

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 2: End User - PDF Report Export
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As an End User,
I want to export reports to PDF format,
So that I can share formatted reports with stakeholders.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Separate from CSV functionality
- Negotiable: Layout and styling adjustable
- Valuable: Enables professional report sharing
- Estimable: PDF generation is well-understood
- Small: Single format export
- Testable: Clear output verification

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in as an End User
  When I view a report
  Then I see an "Export to PDF" button
  When I click "Export to PDF"
  Then the report downloads as a formatted PDF file
  And the PDF includes report title, date range, and data tables

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 3: Power User - Filtered Report Export
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As a Power User,
I want to export reports with applied filters and date ranges,
So that I can export only the relevant data subset.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Builds on base export functionality
- Negotiable: Filter options can be prioritized
- Valuable: Reduces data processing time
- Estimable: Filter application is defined
- Small: Filter integration only
- Testable: Export matches filter criteria

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in as a Power User
  When I apply filters to a report (date range, status, category)
  Then I see the filtered results
  When I click "Export"
  Then the exported file contains only filtered data
  And the export includes a note about applied filters

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 4: Administrator - Export Activity Audit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As an Administrator,
I want to view a log of all report exports,
So that I can audit data access and compliance.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Audit trail separate from export UI
- Negotiable: Log fields can be adjusted
- Valuable: Enables compliance and security monitoring
- Estimable: Logging implementation is standard
- Small: Audit log view only
- Testable: Logs accurately reflect export activity

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in as an Administrator
  When I navigate to the Audit Logs section
  Then I see a list of all report export activities
  And each log entry shows: user, report name, export format, timestamp
  When I filter by date range
  Then only exports within that range are displayed

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 5: Administrator - Export Permissions Management
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As an Administrator,
I want to configure which users can export reports,
So that I can control data access by role.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Permission system separate from export
- Negotiable: Permission levels negotiable
- Valuable: Controls sensitive data exposure
- Estimable: Permission UI and backend defined
- Small: Toggle-based permission system
- Testable: Permissions enforce correctly

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in as an Administrator
  When I navigate to User Permissions
  Then I see a toggle for "Report Export" per user/role
  When I disable export for a user
  Then that user cannot see export buttons
  When I enable export for a user
  Then that user sees export functionality

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STORY 6: System - Export Notification
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
As a User,
I want to receive confirmation when an export is complete,
So that I know the export succeeded.

INVEST Compliance:
- Independent: Notification layer
- Negotiable: Notification method adjustable
- Valuable: Provides user feedback
- Estimable: Simple toast/notification implementation
- Small: Single notification type
- Testable: Notification appears on success/failure

Acceptance Criteria (Given-When-Then):
  Given I am logged in
  When I initiate a report export
  Then I see a progress indicator
  When the export completes successfully
  Then I see a success notification
  When the export fails
  Then I see an error notification with reason

================================================================================
END OF EPIC BREAKDOWN
================================================================================
EOF

